\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Key Takeaways\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The "Model / Context / Protocol" name directly maps to the 3-stage origin story:
\f1\b0  
\f4\i Model
\f1\i0  = the original black-box LLM that could only answer; 
\f4\i Context
\f1\i0  = giving the model more to see (so its answers are better); 
\f4\i Protocol
\f1\i0  = the standardized client/host/server "language" that lets any AI application plug into any compliant tool provider without custom, duplicated integration code.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 MCP's core value proposition is 
\f0\b eliminating duplicated, fragile, hard-to-secure tool-wrapper code across teams/companies
\f1\b0 , not adding new model intelligence.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Host \uc0\u8594  Client \u8594  Server
\f1\b0 , with the 
\f0\b SIM card analogy
\f1\b0  as the recommended mental model over the commonly-cited (and, per the instructor, oversimplified) "USB-C port" analogy.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Three MCP primitives: 
\f0\b Tools, Resources, Prompts
\f1\b0  \'97 only Tools were explored in real depth this session; Resources and Prompts are explicitly deferred to upcoming classes.\
\ls11\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Transport: 
\f0\b STDIO
\f1\b0  (local) vs. 
\f0\b Streamable HTTP
\f1\b0  (remote) \'97 HTTP+SSE is deprecated (spec update, March 2025).\
\ls11\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Next classes will cover: MCP architecture in full depth, 
\f0\b building your own MCP server and client from scratch
\f1\b0 , and 
\f0\b publishing an MCP server as an installable package
\f1\b0  (e.g., to PyPI) \'97 explicitly framed as the target "interview-grade" depth for this unit, before circling back to LangChain-specific MCP integration.\
